WEBVTT

1
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Nathan B.: Launch readiness. The pricing page is done, the launch email is drafted, and billing has one open case: clinics mid-trial on the old plan.

2
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Emma C.: And Shah's support macros for self-serve signups are ready for launch day.

3
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:37.000
Nathan B.: Every blocker we raised since 5 October is now closed or owned with a date.

4
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.000
Anna H.: On billing: we'll handle the mid-trial case in billing by Thursday.

5
00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:20.000
Emma C.: And the billing FAQ should say what happens mid-trial.

6
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:54.000
Nathan B.: Decision: clinics mid-trial keep their old trial terms, and the new pricing applies from their first invoice.

7
00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:27.000
Anna H.: Then billing changes freeze on 23 October, three days before go/no-go.

8
00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.000
Nathan B.: Agreed.

9
00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:28.000
Anna H.: Incident follow-up: the per-clinic rate limits are live. The five-minute alert ships Wednesday.

10
00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:16.000
Nathan B.: I'll run the go/no-go Monday morning, everyone brings their checklist.

11
00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:08.000
Daniel K.: Onboarding: calendar connects in the email test are at 79% versus 72%.
